      <Desc>LEEP WORKS TO ELIMINATE CHILDHOOD LEAD POISONING FROM PAINT BY GENERATING EVIDENCE, STRENGTHENING REGULATION, AND SUPPORTING INDUSTRY REFORMULATION. IN FY25, LEEP COMPLETED PAINT STUDIES IN 4 COUNTRIES COTE DIVOIRE, RWANDA, MALAWI, AND PAKISTAN AND SHARED RESULTS WITH KEY STAKEHOLDERS TO IDENTIFY WHERE LEAD PAINT REMAINS AVAILABLE ON THE MARKET, GUIDING TARGETED PROGRAM INTERVENTIONS. LEEP-INITIATED PAINT PROGRAMS LAUNCHED IN 11 NEW COUNTRIES FOLLOWING LEEPS STUDIES AND SUPPORT, 6 COUNTRIES ANNOUNCED INTENTIONS TO INTRODUCE LEAD PAINT REGULATION, AND 2 COUNTRIES INTRODUCED REGULATION. LEEP ALSO PROVIDED TECHNICAL ASSISTANCE TO HELP PAINT MANUFACTURERS REFORMULATE, ENGAGING THE VAST MAJORITY OF LEAD PAINT MANUFACTURERS BY MARKET SHARE IN 9 COUNTRIES - IN 2 OF THOSE COUNTRIES, MORE THAN 50 OF MARKET SHARE TOOK ACTIVE REFORMULATION STEPS, AND IN 1 COUNTRY, 100 OF MARKET SHARE DID SO. SEE SCHEDULE O</Desc>
